{
  "knob": 4,
  "name": "KV cache eviction",
  "regime": 1,
  "n": 1000,
  "reference": "evict_none_b1",
  "batch_size": 1,
  "transformers": "5.0.0",
  "policies": [
    "recency",
    "sink_recent",
    "random",
    "attention"
  ],
  "keep_ratios": {
    "short": [
      0.75,
      0.5,
      0.25
    ],
    "explain": [
      0.5,
      0.25
    ]
  },
  "frozen_constants": {
    "sink": 4,
    "seed": 42,
    "shift_rope": true,
    "top_k": 5
  },
  "arms": {
    "short": "results/knob4_short_summary.json",
    "explain": "results/knob4_explain_summary.json",
    "retention": "results/knob4_retention_summary.json"
  },
  "predictions": {
    "efficiency_null": {
      "registered": "Eviction imposes a measurable quality cost against an efficiency benefit that does not materialise at this scale: eviction acts after prefill, peak memory occurs during prefill.",
      "outcome": "CONFIRMED. Peak memory 6.11-6.15 GiB across all settings against 5.87 GiB of weights; evicting 75% of the cache moved peak by 0.02 GiB (0.3%). Quality cost is large and significant at every setting."
    },
    "rope_shift_small": {
      "registered": "RoPE position-shifting matters LESS at ~744 tokens than in the long-context literature, where holes span millions of tokens.",
      "outcome": "CONFIRMED in the strongest available form. Paired shifted vs naive: b=0 c=0, identical marginals (EM 0.2820 both). 32/1000 predictions changed, none changed correctness."
    },
    "attention_beats_position": {
      "registered": "Attention-based eviction beats position-based at equal keep_ratio, because gold evidence sits mid-prompt.",
      "outcome": "CONFIRMED in short mode at r0.50 and r0.25 (p<0.0001 both), null at r0.75 (p=0.1550). Confirmed in explain at r0.25 (p=0.0003), null at r0.50 (p=0.0630). But the STATED REASON is falsified \u2014 see gold_retention below."
    },
    "attention_beats_random": {
      "registered": "Implied: content-aware selection separates from a coin flip.",
      "outcome": "BUDGET-DEPENDENT. Short mode: p=0.3317 (r0.75), p=0.1074 (r0.50), b=226 c=14 p<0.0001 (r0.25). Initially recorded as FALSIFIED from r0.50 alone; the amendment adding r0.75 and r0.25 showed the separation exists at tight budgets. A single-budget control cannot support a claim about a budget-dependent mechanism."
    },
    "gold_retention": {
      "registered": "Attention wins BECAUSE it retains gold-passage tokens better than position policies do.",
      "outcome": "FALSIFIED. Gold-span retention, attention vs random: 0.294 vs 0.496 (r0.50), 0.091 vs 0.230 (r0.25). Attention retains LESS gold and scores HIGHER EM. Rank correlation between gold retention and EM flips sign by budget: +0.678 (r0.50), -0.581 (r0.25). What predicts quality is retention of the QUESTION, not the evidence."
    },
    "explain_amplification": {
      "registered": "Following knob 3: a longer decode amplifies cache damage.",
      "outcome": "CONFIRMED at roughly 10x knob 3's magnitude. Paired on the 307 questions both references answer correctly, explain-only-broken vs short-only-broken: 88/0, 168/0, 60/2, 196/8, 123/0, 174/0, 181/7, 235/2. All p<0.0001."
    }
  },
  "findings": [
    "Eviction is a large, significant quality cost at every setting, against a measured efficiency benefit of ~0.3% peak memory. Direct evidence for open question 1: the long-context KV literature's assumptions do not transfer to short-context RAG.",
    "What eviction destroys first is the ability to POSE THE TASK, not access to evidence. At r0.25 all four policies have lost 90-95% of the gold span, yet short-mode EM ranges 0.087-0.299. Question-span retention separates them: recency/sink 1.000, attention 0.975, random 0.224.",
    "In explain mode the dominant failure is FORMAT ADHERENCE. Among generations that stopped cleanly, parse rate is 1.000 at the reference vs 0.058-0.507 under eviction. The model terminates fluently and never emits the answer marker.",
    "NO POLICY DOMINATES across budget and decode length. Short: attention wins at r0.25/r0.50, random collapses at r0.25. Explain: attention wins at r0.25, random wins EM at r0.50 while truncating on 39% of questions vs attention's 2.5%.",
    "Retrieval rank and eviction survival are COUPLED through prompt position: gold passages rank early, so position policies cut them first (recency distractor retention 0.727 vs gold 0.128 at r0.50). A confound absent from regime 2's pooled corpus, relevant to the Phase 4 knob1 x knob4 surface."
  ],
  "corrections": [
    "rope_scaling is None was the wrong precondition: in transformers 5.0.0 it aliases rope_parameters, always populated. Correct condition is rope_type in (default, linear, yarn, llama3), i.e. inv_freq fixed for the run.",
    "Decoded tokens are not a valid instrument for numerical differences on a random-init model; greedy argmax is near-degenerate there. Logits, and the direct rotation identity check, are the instruments.",
    "A notebook-23 summary line reported 'eager confound exists: True', counting a NaN failure as a numerics difference. Two distinct phenomena conflated.",
    "A full forward materialises logits for every position and OOMs; generate() slices to the last position. Read hidden states off the base model for per-row NaN diagnosis.",
    "Three vacuous tests in sequence: comparing `phase` (the packing invariant forces it identical across layers), asserting on exception TYPE alone (wrong guard fired), and deriving the stub's inv_freq from the head_dim under test. Pattern recorded: a guard test must demonstrate the negative case, not merely go green.",
    "The first verdict helper tested discordant >= 30 before discordant == 0, printing UNINFORMATIVE for the zero-discordant case the knob-5 amendment carves out as a NULL.",
    "max_new_tokens=N yields N tokens but N-1 cache appends; endpoints must be derived from cumulative_length.",
    "evict_sink4_r050 and its naive twin produced identical aggregate EM, b and c while differing on 32/1000 predictions \u2014 a concrete instance of why the acceptance criterion is paired McNemar and never the aggregate gap."
  ],
